<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Voorcompagnieën</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as voorcompagnieen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The voorcompagnieën, or pre-companies, were the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> trading companies formed in the 1590s to send ships to Asia before the creation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>. Their competition drove up prices in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and lowered profits in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. In 1602 the States-General consolidated them into the VOC, which received a monopoly over Dutch trade east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-of-good-hope">Cape of Good Hope</a>.</p></div>
